# 3. The Local-First Philosophy

ORION is designed around a **local-first architecture**.

That means the default assumption is:

> “Do as much as possible on the user's own machine.”

The local layer can handle things such as:

* normal conversation;
* classification;
* intent detection;
* lightweight reasoning;
* local RAG;
* memory retrieval;
* document processing;
* summarization;
* simple coding assistance;
* routing;
* tool selection;
* basic planning.

The local model can run using Ollama.

Depending on hardware, ORION can use a small model such as a lightweight Qwen, Llama or Gemma variant.

The purpose is not necessarily to make the local model the smartest model.

The purpose is to make it:

> **fast, private, available and inexpensive.**

