# 4. Cloud Escalation

When the local model is insufficient, ORION can escalate to the cloud.

For example:

```text
Simple question
      ↓
Local model
      ↓
Answer

Complex research
      ↓
Local classifier
      ↓
"Requires stronger reasoning"
      ↓
OpenRouter
      ↓
Stronger cloud model
      ↓
Return result
```

This is called **cloud escalation**.

The user does not necessarily need to decide manually which model to use.

ORION can determine that from the task.

For example:

### Task A

> “Rewrite this paragraph professionally.”

Local model.

### Task B

> “Summarize these three documents.”

Local model + RAG.

### Task C

> “Analyze this 40,000-line codebase, identify architectural issues, design a migration and generate an implementation plan.”

Likely cloud escalation or a stronger local model.

### Task D

> “Run this browser workflow and update my project.”

Use an agent + browser tools + potentially a stronger reasoning model.

The model router therefore becomes a critical subsystem.

