# 5. The Model Router

The model router is not simply:

> “Randomly pick an AI.”

It evaluates the task.

Possible signals include:

* task category;
* complexity;
* token requirements;
* context size;
* privacy level;
* whether tools are required;
* whether images/audio are involved;
* local hardware availability;
* current provider availability;
* quota limitations;
* historical model performance.

A simplified decision could be:

```text
                    USER REQUEST
                         │
                         ▼
                 INTENT CLASSIFIER
                         │
           ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
           ▼             ▼             ▼
        SIMPLE         COMPLEX      SENSITIVE
           │             │             │
           ▼             ▼             ▼
         LOCAL        CLOUD        LOCAL ONLY
```

This makes ORION both more efficient and less expensive.

