# 7. ORION's RAG System

RAG means:

> Retrieval-Augmented Generation.

Instead of forcing the AI to rely entirely on what it remembers from model training, ORION can retrieve information from the user's own data.

The pipeline is roughly:

```text
User question
      ↓
Intent analysis
      ↓
Query generation
      ↓
Memory search
      ↓
Knowledge search
      ↓
Vector similarity
      +
Full-text search
      ↓
Ranking
      ↓
Context selection
      ↓
AI model
      ↓
Answer with sources
```

For example, the user asks:

> “What did we decide about ORION's authentication system last month?”

ORION can search:

* previous task summaries;
* project documents;
* architecture files;
* stored decisions;
* indexed conversations.

It then presents the relevant evidence to the model.

