# 12. Verification

ORION is designed not to blindly trust its own output.

For important tasks it can ask:

> “What does success look like?”

For example, coding task:

```text
Acceptance Criteria

✓ Code compiles
✓ Tests pass
✓ No critical lint errors
✓ API endpoint responds correctly
✓ Database migration succeeds
```

Research task:

```text
Acceptance Criteria

✓ Required sources found
✓ Information is sufficiently current
✓ Contradictory evidence checked
✓ Claims have supporting sources
```

Browser task:

```text
Acceptance Criteria

✓ Correct website
✓ Correct account
✓ Correct object modified
✓ Expected confirmation observed
```

The verifier can reject an incomplete answer and send the task back for revision.

