# 52. ORION's Internal Philosophy

The system is designed around several principles:

### Local first

Prefer local computation whenever practical.

### Model agnostic

Never make the entire system dependent on one AI provider.

### Tool mediated

The AI never receives unrestricted computer access.

### Human controlled

Important external effects remain subject to explicit permissions.

### Evidence based

Retrieve actual information instead of relying entirely on model memory.

### Verifiable

Important tasks should have acceptance criteria.

### Persistent

Useful knowledge survives individual conversations.

### Modular

Models, databases, MCP servers, connectors and interfaces can be replaced.

### Observable

The user should be able to see what ORION is doing.

### Recoverable

Long-running tasks should be resumable.

